            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life and Education</strong><br>\nStephen Hawking was born on January 8, 1942, in Oxford, England. He studied at the University of Oxford, earning his degree in Natural Sciences. Hawking was renowned for his work in theoretical physics and his efforts to make complex scientific concepts understandable to a wider audience. Despite being diagnosed with Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis (ALS) at the age of 21, he continued his academic work and obtained a Ph.D. in cosmological physics at Cambridge.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Significance of Hawking's Work</strong><br>\nStephen Hawking made significant contributions to our understanding of the universe. His research on black holes led to the theory that they are not completely black but can emit radiation, later known as Hawking radiation. This discovery was revolutionary as it connected quantum mechanics with general relativity.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Hawking Radiation and Black Holes</strong><br>\nHawking radiation was a groundbreaking theory stating that black holes could lose energy due to the effects of quantum fluctuations at their edges, known as event horizons. This contradicted the prevailing belief at the time that nothing, not even light, could escape a black hole. Hawking's theories contributed to expanding our understanding of the end of black holes and the nature of the universe.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "es"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
