          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Time and Space in Hawking's Theories</strong><br>\nStephen Hawking also explored the limits of time and space, proposing the theory that time had a beginning with the Big Bang. He argued that the laws of physics could explain how the universe originated without the need for a creator. His research helped clarify concepts such as the beginning and end of the universe.</p>\n\n<p><strong>A Popular Scientist</strong><br>\nHawking was also known for his ability to communicate complex scientific ideas in a way understandable to the general public. His book \"A Brief History of Time\" became an international bestseller, catapulting him into the public spotlight as a popular scientist. He used his fame to advocate for science and research, promoting public understanding of physics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Struggle with ALS</strong><br>\nDespite his battle with ALS, which significantly limited his mobility over time, Hawking remained scientifically active. With the help of various technical aids, he continued to communicate and work. His ability to triumph despite personal challenges made him a symbol of perseverance and determination.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "es"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
