          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Influence on Modern Physics</strong><br>\nHawking's influence extends far beyond black holes. He worked on theories related to the Big Bang and what is now known as the Hawking-Penrose theorems, describing conditions for the emergence of singularities in the universe. These works have shaped the fields of cosmology and quantum physics and continue to influence how scientists think about the universe.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Hawking and Pop Culture</strong><br>\nStephen Hawking was a fixture in pop culture as well. He appeared in TV shows like \"Star Trek: The Next Generation\" and \"The Simpsons,\" even playing himself. These appearances showcased his sense of humor and willingness to make himself and his work accessible to a broad audience.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Commemoration</strong><br>\nWhen Stephen Hawking passed away on March 14, 2018, he left behind a rich legacy of scientific insights and inspiration. His research is being continued by physicists worldwide, and his life as an outstanding scientist who could make complex theories understandable is taught and celebrated in educational institutions everywhere. Hawking remains one of the defining figures in modern scientific history.</p>\n"
              },
